  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "driver",
      "fact": "The sole concrete constructor retains the exact already-spawned driver cleanup handle in one mandatory Shared<BoxFuture<Result<OriginalDriverJoined,String>>> before publishing the job. The task body and service-cancel match, including unknown QuitReason rejection, are byte unchanged.",
      "cancellation": "Waiters clone the registry-held completion. Dropping a waiter cannot remove the handle or repoll a completed handle. Concurrent observers get the cached original terminal result.",
      "errors": "The actual task's result is unchanged. The pre-existing JoinError-to-string mapping moves verbatim into the shared future; no typed error is newly flattened."
    },
    {
      "id": "startup_cleanup",
      "fact": "OriginalStartupJob and OriginalCleanupJob similarly retain the same existing actual handles in mandatory shared completions. Their registration lock regions contain no new await. The original startup JoinSet drain and always-attempt-client-cleanup body are byte unchanged.",
      "errors": "OriginalStartupJoined already implements Clone; cleanup returns the same Arc observation. All pre-existing actual task failure strings and aggregation order remain. Existing private missing-optional-handle branches become structurally unrepresentable rather than success cases."
    },
    {
